    <DataNode elementId="AT3G46970-MONOMER" textLabel="Alpha-glucan phosphorylase 2, cytosolic" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9SD76" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="615" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">|FRAME: AT3G46970-MONOMER PHS2| (&amp;alpha;-glucan phosphorylase 2) is a cytosolic enzyme involved in |FRAME: PWY-7238 sucrose biosynthesis| in the cytosol. It appears to be indirectly involved in starch degradation. In this process the |FRAME: MALTOSE maltose| released from |FRAME: PWY-6724 starch degradation in the chloroplast| exported via |FRAME: AT5G17520-MONOMER MEX1| is used by |FRAME: AT2G40840-MONOMER DPE2| to attach glucosyl units to the poorly defined class of compounds referred to as |FRAME: Soluble-Heteroglycans Soluble HeteroGlycans| (SHG). |FRAME: AT3G46970-MONOMER PHS2| can then liberate this deposited glucose in the form of |FRAME: GLC-1-P &amp;alpha;-D-glucopyranose 1-phosphate| |CITS: [16980562][23393426][16640603]|. This model is supported by the observation that &lt;i&gt;phs2&lt;/i&gt; mutant plants have elevated levels of maltose at night as well as by &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt; evidence that |FRAME: AT3G46970-MONOMER PHS2| acts on |FRAME: Soluble-Heteroglycans SHG| |CITS: [16980562][16640603]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G46970-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT3G46970.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9SD76" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="AtPHS2" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="Alpha-glucan phosphorylase, H isozyme" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="Starch phosphorylase H" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-21551, RXN-9841, RXN-9840, RXN-ARA-500" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="4" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT3G46970.1" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":PROBABLE-ENZYME" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT3G46970" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
    </DataNode>
