      <Comment source="SRI, caspi">This compound stands for a mixture of |FRAME: ALPHA-GLUCOSE| and |FRAME: GLC|. In most cases, each of these compounds mutarotates quickly to form a mixture of the two, and thus it is the general rule to use this non-specific form in reactions unless it is specifically known that an enzyme can accept only one of the forms.</Comment>
